# Next steps for {{ workspace_name }}

Your workspace is bootstrapped. The canonical PR flow walks from this empty
state through importing existing models, adding your own model, pulling
processes, capturing expert input, building a baseline, and implementing
phases of model extension. Each stage lands as its own PR.

Tick boxes as you go.

## Setup (now)

- [ ] `git init && git add -A && git commit -m "feat(stage-0): workspace bootstrap"`
- [ ] `uv venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate && uv pip install -e ".[dev]"`
- [ ] `python scripts/lint-workspace.py` should print `workspace lint: OK`
- [ ] Push to GitHub: `gh repo create <org>/{{ workspace_name }} --public --source=. --remote=origin --push`

## Stage 0.5 — Import existing models *(optional)*

If your project builds on an existing model (e.g., `vivarium-collective/v2ecoli`),
register it here. Three modes:

- **reference** — read-only submodule under `external/<name>/` for citation,
  comparison, or per-file cherry-pick.
- **fork-source** — catalog-only seed for a future `/pbg-add-model --from-import`
  (no checkout yet).
- **in-place** — submodule under `models/<name>/` with `external: true`; you
  operate against an external repo and PRs from this workspace open against
  the upstream remote.

Workflow:

- [ ] *(plugin path)* `/pbg-import-models <name> --source <url> --ref <ref> --mode <reference|fork-source|in-place>`
- [ ] *(no-plugin path)* edit `workspace.yaml.imports` directly + run
      `git submodule add <source> external/<name>` (or `models/<name>` for in-place mode)

Full lifecycle: `pbg-superpowers/skills/pbg-import-models/SKILL.md`.

## Stage 1+2 — Add a model

Each model lives under `models/<name>/` as a git submodule (its own GitHub repo).

- [ ] Scaffold from the model template (in `pbg-superpowers/templates/model/`) into a fresh sibling dir, e.g. `~/code/<name>/`
- [ ] In that dir: `git init && git add -A && git commit -m "feat(M3-stage-2): model package scaffold"`, then `gh repo create <org>/<name> --public --source=. --remote=origin --push`
- [ ] Back in the workspace: `git submodule add https://github.com/<org>/<name>.git models/<name>`
- [ ] Add the entry under `workspace.yaml.models.<name>` (`submodule_path`, `remote`, `pbg_processes: []`, `stages.add_model.status: complete`)
- [ ] `python scripts/lint-workspace.py` to confirm

Full lifecycle: `pbg-superpowers/skills/pbg-add-model/SKILL.md`.

## Stages 3 – 9..N

| Stage | What | SKILL.md |
|---|---|---|
| 3 | Pull required `pbg-*` wrappers; register them in `models/<name>/pbg_<slug>/core.py` | `pbg-pull-processes/SKILL.md` |
| 4+5 | Add datasets to `datasets/_index.yaml`; references to `references/papers.bib` + `claims.yaml` | `pbg-data/SKILL.md` |
| 6 | Capture expert expectations as `if X then Y` acceptance tests | `pbg-expert-input/SKILL.md` |
| 7 | Build minimal end-to-end Composite; persist registry snapshot to `tests/registry-snapshot.json` | `pbg-baseline/SKILL.md` |
| 8 | Lay out N phases using the Phase Template | `pbg-phase-plan/SKILL.md` |
| 9..N | Implement each phase; run the Phase Gate before moving to the next | `pbg-phase/SKILL.md` |

Full design: see `pbg-superpowers/docs/superpowers/specs/`.

## Two paths

- **With Claude Code + the [pbg-superpowers plugin](https://github.com/vivarium-collective/pbg-superpowers):**
  every stage above is a `/pbg-*` skill that walks the interactive flow and
  opens a clean PR.
- **Without the plugin:** open the relevant `SKILL.md` and follow the
  9-phase lifecycle manually. Run `python scripts/lint-workspace.py` after
  every change.

## Config files to know

- `workspace.yaml` — canonical state (models registered, imports catalog, stage status per model)
- `docs/decisions.yaml` — append-only design log; every stage skill writes here
- `references/{papers.bib, claims.yaml}` — bibliography + claim → paper mapping
- `datasets/_index.yaml` — dataset registry
- `.pbg/schemas/` — workspace + phase JSON schemas (used by `lint-workspace.py`)

## When stuck

1. Run `python scripts/lint-workspace.py` — most workspace-shape issues surface here.
2. Open the relevant `SKILL.md` in `pbg-superpowers/skills/`.
3. File an issue at <https://github.com/vivarium-collective/pbg-superpowers/issues>.
